{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars","id":280860,"title":"Why do you like Lunars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-14T04:55:32-07:00","id":280860,"title":"Why do you like Lunars?","content":"So, after the good reaction for the same topic about Dragoonblooded I decided to ask about my favorite gameline - Lunars.<br /> Note: I deslike 1 ed Lunars, cuz their &quot;kill-rape-burn-be-true-savagers&quot; idea, but the second ed are very good for me.<br /> Reasons:<br /> 1) Shifting<br /> 2) Social experiments<br /> 3) They are quite bad-ass and can fight against and can be fighters equal to everyone up to and including Abyssals.<br /> So, what is your reasons? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:53:12-07:00","id":280913,"title":"","content":"Nobody like Lunars? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:53:20-07:00","id":280914,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily in any particular order:<br /> <br /> 1) Shifting<br /> 2) I like the relative morality antihero vibe they bring in in opposition to solars' absolutism, in the what-should-be vs. what-needs-to-be sense.<br /> 3) Eating people<br /> 3.5) ... and their memories/fates<br /> 3.75) ... and posing as them to gain a foot-hold in an organisation<br /> 3.875) ... and eventually replacing everyone, going crazy, and forgetting that the other people in the organisation are also you. Getting mad at them for not doing things.<br /> 4) Versatile powers that can be applied in creative ways<br /> 5) Beautiful white bird / Flies over its enemies / Transforms into whale.<br /> <br /> [I may edit this post if I find more things to add]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:58:27-07:00","id":280918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280914#post280914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Beautiful white bird / Flies over its enemies / Transforms into whale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I'd forgotten that was a thing that happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:02:13-07:00","id":280922,"title":"","content":"Thematically I like playing something that's a bit otherworldly that stops short of being alien. Raksha are a bit too alien while Abyssals and Infernals both come with &quot;baggage&quot; that stop me from really making the most of that aspect of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:16:03-07:00","id":280928,"title":"","content":"Where else can I transform into a giant trapdoor spider, bind creatures from all corners of existence (and the Wyld) in magical spider-silk from my own flesh, weave flesh and bone using the quasi-fabric of the Moon's light and the other-rules of the Beyond, and emerge from the ground with a hundred occidental dragons and an army of beastmen as Ardent Fang, Bolt-Weaver, Dragon-Spider, Forger of The Dragonflight, Father of a Thousand Young?<br /> <br /> Odd, right. Even playing as an Infernal, the closest I've gotten to being a trueEldritch Abomination is right here, in Lunar Town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:25:58-07:00","id":280930,"title":"","content":"I've always liked heroes with many faces, both physical and psychological. I am the chaos-born seducer, I am the mother of all beasts, I am the Void-slaying light and the creature lurking in the shadows, I hunt with the wolves and run with the hinds- because I am <i>Lunar</i>, and no form or rule can contain me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:26:25-07:00","id":280936,"title":"","content":"I like shapeshifting, because it's a versatile tool that can be used in a lot of situations, but involves a little thought. It's not just &quot;use X charm, solve X problem&quot;. Kind of like Sidereals-lite.<br /> I like the monstrous but not to the extent of being demonic stuff. DBT, eating hearts, etc.<br /> I like the way their charms work, in that you tend to be good at a lot of stuff but not game-breakingly good. It makes it easy to run a game for them.<br /> I like the fact that you can build a character around a strong, basic concept: an animal. You pick an animal, eke out all of its connotations, and bam, character. Tenacious but greedy boar man, treacherous and manipulative snake totem guy, sexy but lazy cat girl, black dog necromancer who guards the barrier between life and death, southern pyromancer with a salamander totem, etc, etc. Bam. It gives you a lot to work with from an easy base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:44:57-07:00","id":280940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280936#post280936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like shapeshifting, because it's a versatile tool that can be used in a lot of situations, but involves a little thought. It's not just &quot;use X charm, solve X problem&quot;. Kind of like Sidereals-lite.<br /> I like the monstrous but not to the extent of being demonic stuff. DBT, eating hearts, etc.<br /> I like the way their charms work, in that you tend to be good at a lot of stuff but not game-breakingly good. It makes it easy to run a game for them.<br /> I like the fact that you can build a character around a strong, basic concept: an animal. You pick an animal, eke out all of its connotations, and bam, character. Tenacious but greedy boar man, treacherous and manipulative snake totem guy, sexy but lazy cat girl, black dog necromancer who guards the barrier between life and death, southern pyromancer with a salamander totem, etc, etc. Bam. It gives you a lot to work with from an easy base.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this, and to add: I like that you can get surprising combinations out of it too, e.g.: crocodile changing-moon that is patient and brutal in social combat.<br /> Crocs usually go to Full-moons, but the fact that they are hunted for their skin makes them also fall into changing-moon territory.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: I like territory charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:24:38-07:00","id":280985,"title":"","content":"I like:<br /> <br /> -Shapeshifting, flat out - I love OWoD Werewolf/Fera; DBT is Crinos and I love the option even if it shouldn't be mandatory to be effective<br /> -The notion that your powers are based on your innate characteristics rather than learned skills - and you can boost your inherent characteristics just as easily as many people boost their learned skills<br /> -Their Incarna comes off as competent but realistically distant and not just as a big mopey jerk<br /> -Gaining power through eating hearts (a huge thing both in IRL cultures and in fantasy fiction about eating your enemy's heart/soul to gain their strength)<br /> -Charms like River Reflects Desire (people look at you and see the person they most want to see in that moment) and Dreams and Expectations Stance (people look at you and see the person they most expect to see in that moment) - basically screwing with perceptions and changing what you portray even if your shape is technically the same<br /> -Being Other from every society, yet effortlessly incorporating into any of them as needed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280940#post280940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the fact that they are hunted for their skin makes them also fall into changing-moon territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can basically shoehorn any animal form into being appropriate for any Caste. Hell, the book basically does it for you with big cats and snakes. Really those &quot;guidelines&quot; on &quot;what spirit shape generally goes with what Caste&quot; were worthless except to help people see how pretty much any animal can thematically fit anywhere if you think about it enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280913#post280913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody like Lunars? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe don't bump a thread after it's been open for one hour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:32:21-07:00","id":280991,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the primal, wild heroes of folklore; Enkidu, Sun Wukong, and the like. In addition, I've found it quite easy to visualize how shape-shifting can assist in any given situation, making it amusing in that several times the Solars of the circle had trouble keeping up with all the myriad benefits that my Lunar's protean forms gave them. <br /> <br /> That, and at the end of the story, I can become a gigantic monster, which is always neat, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:33:25-07:00","id":281036,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf links are a big part of it. They also put a weird kink in the wuxia roll that a lot of other splats produce, being all about capabilities instead of training. Most folk don't challenge the wuxia hero type successfully if they rely first and foremost on strength, speed, etc. Lunars, however, can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:37:08-07:00","id":281039,"title":"","content":"The only reason I like Lunars is because anthro animals are hot, eh, too shallow ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:38:34-07:00","id":281041,"title":"","content":"While it might be an unpopular view of them, one of my favorite things about lunars is their total lack &quot;to do lists&quot;.<br /> <br /> Due to charm mechanics, Lunars are not expected to save all of Creation like Solars.<br /> <br /> Due to storyline design, Lunars are not expected to destroy all of Creation like Abyssals or to a certain extent Infernals.<br /> <br /> Other than ducking Wyld Hunts and occasionally listening to the elders, Lunars don't have any pre-existing jobs as soon as they exalt, like say the Sidereals or Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> They are more powerful than Dragon-Blooded and can go the whole breeding a better race storyline route, but don't have all the family drama.<br /> <br /> Lunars are just as transhumanist as Alchemicals, but they don't have the infrastructure requirements nor the nationalist storyline baggage.<br /> <br /> In fact one could argue that they even side step many of the over used tropes of the exalted setting because of their design. For example there is really very little reason to visit a previous exaltation holders tomb. Lunars benefit the least from artifacts and infrastructure and as such getting equipped is more of a storyline concept than a requirement like it is with most other exalt types.<br /> <br /> So with all of this in mind, Lunars are the most adaptable splat from a storytelling standpoint. They can be scientists, they can be major threats to civilization, they can be honorable warriors, they can Sorcerers or Necromancers, they can be barbarians or they can be high society socialites, etc. etc. etc. The list goes on and on of all the things you can do with a Lunar character and not really be outside the realm of probability for the splat.<br /> <br /> While this total lack of &quot;to do lists&quot; can, by some unimaginative types, be considered a weakness of the splat, I personally find it refreshing since every other splat seems to have a predestined intended place in the meta of Exalted. Solars save the world, Abyssals &amp; Infernals end it, Sidereals have ego issues and mismanage everything, Terrestrials are cannon fodder who can't do their jobs on their own, and Alchemicals exist to bait Steam Punk/Tech enthusiasts sales.<br /> <br /> This lack of pre-existing storyline pretty much means that an all Lunar pack/circle can play in any game style, any storyline theme or any level of seriousness and still make sense. Because they were never stuck in the Jade Prison like the Solar Exaltations (and those that would become Abyssals &amp; Infernals) it means your storyline can take place during any time from the Primordial War to the beginning of the Third Age. Their hibernation charms even keep book keeping clean when it comes to skipping ahead in the timeline.<br /> <br /> All in all I think Lunars are my favorite splat for playing games that are Skyrim-esque, in that you can just go exploring and enjoy the game play rather than being forced into a particular role or a given storyline or even a time table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:06:00-07:00","id":281216,"title":"","content":"I back Thoth on this. One of the Lunar's things, that might be helpful to emphasize if you go down that route, is them <i>not</i> doing things together as a splat. If the Silver Pact must still be a thing, say that it's a recent thing and it's not a thing that's working out very well because Lunar's don't have any encouragement toward splat loyalty. Except the tats, hate the tats. Kinda like TAW's version of the Silver Pact, it's mostly very old, very bitter men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:09:35-07:00","id":281218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars#post280860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after the good reaction for the same topic about Dragoonblooded I decided to ask about my favorite gameline - Lunars.<br /> Note: I deslike 1 ed Lunars, cuz their &quot;kill-rape-burn-be-true-savagers&quot; idea, but the second ed are very good for me.<br /> Reasons:<br /> <br /> 2) Social experiments</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thousand Streams River has been confirmed as not coming back in 3e (in fact, it was confirmed as axed back in 2e, as in &quot;will never be mentioned again.&quot;)<br /> <br /> While some Lunars do those things, I don't think it makes sense as a default way Lunars in particular interact with the world -- they're no more into social experiments than Sidereals are, say (in fact, Sidereals probably do a lot more of it, since they're the intellectual driven-by-reason Robespierre types.) And of course Solars do a lot of it as well. Which isn't to say that Lunars <i>don't</i>, it's just that it never made much sense to make that the Lunar &quot;thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) They are quite bad-ass and can fight against and can be fighters equal to everyone up to and including Abyssals. </div> </div> </div>So can everyone else. &quot;Lunars NUMBAH ONE&quot; was never a workable concept; all of the Exalted are badass and dangerous fighters in their own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:26:21-07:00","id":281226,"title":"","content":"Several reasons really, lets see:<br /> <br /> 1. You know that guy in the band who's not the lead singer but is just as cool (the Slash for every Axl)? Well, in a setting plagued by unending lines about how awesomely awesome, important, significant, powerful are the solars, lunars occupy that place in my perception of the setting. Sure solars get most of the spotlight but... there's always these guys in the background that don't give a damn if writers make them justice, cause we all know they are cool as hell.<br /> <br /> 2. Animals. I'm a biologist and an illustrator, so lunars give me both a chance to implement strange biological aesthetics and themes to characters: the alligator shaman in the swamp, the photosynthetic mollusk undersea sage, the sparrow ninja with the poisonous feathers, etc.<br /> <br /> 3. Rivalry. Yep, lunars above other exalts hold this special potential to become a solars best buddy or biggest rival. Sure you can have an abyssal playing that part, but he's more like a bizarro or shadow rival. This is why I've always liked the idea of pushing lunar power level above sidereals, and let them have their own strange way to rival the absolute power of the solar. I wanna read about how when the old golden king of the first age went mad, it was his silver comrade that took him down for the sake of the kingdom, and not just how impossible or unlikely this would'be been given the stats and systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 10-14-2014, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:34:23-07:00","id":281238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281041#post281041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to charm mechanics, Lunars are not expected to save all of Creation like Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad Solar mechanics were bad. There's a middle ground between &quot;their magic is necessary for the greatest glories to exist&quot; and &quot;they basically did jack shit for 2000 years and act like mopey losers that whole time.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281041#post281041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that you can just go exploring and enjoy the game play rather than being forced into a particular role or a given storyline or even a time table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get how this is a Lunar-specific game theme. Any splat could do this; it's more of a general game premise and storytelling model than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:02:42-07:00","id":281277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281238#post281238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get how this is a Lunar-specific game theme. Any splat could do this; it's more of a general game premise and storytelling model than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the idea that people, regardless how open minded or innovative they are, see splat types in certain terms.<br /> <br /> If a player goes with a solar, you kind of automatically expect them to:<br /> 1. go to their old tomb to gear up.<br /> 2. Bring their circle together<br /> 3. Be the best at their niche &quot;thing&quot;<br /> 4. Change the course of history<br /> 5. Reinvent the First Age or go off into the Wyld and build a new world.<br /> <br /> If a player chooses to play a Lunar, they can do all of the above or they are equally likely to turn into a cat, curl up into a ball and sleep through the adventure.<br /> <br /> Because Lunars have so few storyline requirements nearly any form of behavior is appropriate, add in the fact that they turn into animals and basically any internet vid of animals doing goofy things becomes a role play guide.<br /> <br /> So Lunars basically become the perfect character splat for people with ADD or commitment issues since what ever random thing takes their fancy is thematically correct for the exalt type. Obviously Lunars are good for other player types, but they really have the least back story to know, the simplest of reasons to come together and have the least on-rails expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:21:31-07:00","id":281290,"title":"","content":"I have rolled this question around in my head for a very long time. I'm no longer completely sure I <i>do</i> like them; I may have just been in &quot;I <i>want</i> to like them&quot; territory for a while. We'll see how they shape up in EX3.<br /> <br /> Regardless, reasons for liking or wanting to like them may include:<br /> - The Lancer: I've never had a lot of drive or attraction toward being the star of the show (or at least a traditional one). But I do get a lot of personal satisfaction from supporting something or someone I care about. Even if the implementation was rocky, there's an element of that in Lunars that speaks to me.<br /> - Animal Symbolism: What can I say? I've always been a sucker for this stuff. Whether playing it straight or playing with expectations, I enjoy myself when it presents itself.<br /> - Shapeshifting: Just a very fun, flexible, and powerful capability they've got, straight out of the box. Could do with more options for changing others, but still, cool stuff I rather enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281238#post281238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get how this is a Lunar-specific game theme. Any splat could do this; it's more of a general game premise and storytelling model than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my take, too. Almost every splat can just go in for general exploration and game play just fine, or they can go in for their respective splat-specific narratives. Lunars don't have a meaningfully distinct splat-specific narrative in 2e, so this comes across to me as fewer options, not more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:59:40-07:00","id":281337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Thousand Streams River has been confirmed as not coming back in 3e (in fact, it was confirmed as axed back in 2e, as in &quot;will never be mentioned again.&quot;) </div> </div> </div>And that still depresses me.<br /> <br /> Thousand Streams River.... whilst not exactly the main thing I liked about Lunars was very evocative of it. They had options. Well, all splats have those to some degree, but Lunars had existed as a society largely apart from Creation and the Realm. And that meant they could interact with those things in ways other groups couldn't. More than any other splat they felt like they had potentail for individuality. Sidereals are bound to make sure Fate works, DBs aren't bound to anything specifically but usually have very close ties to a specific nation. Infernals and Abyssals have their masters to serve or rail against, and Solars have kinda a preordained path to a point.<br /> <br /> But Lunars?<br /> <br /> A Crossroads Society member could try to institute a program of education amongst the slaves of Deshan. Another could create a nation of illiterate monkey slaves to serve her every whim as she continued her personal studies into Solar Circle Sorcery. You could get a Lunar Guildsman in Nexus selling slaves to Malfeas, or a Lunar Tribesman breaking up those same caravans. All of that's consistant with the Silver Pact. They're all the same people. They just don't have a narrative they're bound to.<br /> <br /> Lunars had infinite variety. They could be tricksters, or monsters, heroes or villains. They could stand for anything or anyone or they could tear down whatever part of the world offended them. And that's what I loved about them.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if this is negative. Trying not to start a flame war, but... 3E Lunars just depress me thus far.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:22:53-07:00","id":281364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281337#post281337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that still depresses me.<br /> <br /> Thousand Streams River.... whilst not exactly the main thing I liked about Lunars was very evocative of it. They had options. Well, all splats have those to some degree, but Lunars had existed as a society largely apart from Creation and the Realm. And that meant they could interact with those things in ways other groups couldn't. More than any other splat they felt like they had potentail for individuality. Sidereals are bound to make sure Fate works, DBs aren't bound to anything specifically but usually have very close ties to a specific nation. Infernals and Abyssals have their masters to serve or rail against, and Solars have kinda a preordained path to a point.<br /> <br /> But Lunars?<br /> <br /> A Crossroads Society member could try to institute a program of education amongst the slaves of Deshan. Another could create a nation of illiterate monkey slaves to serve her every whim as she continued her personal studies into Solar Circle Sorcery. You could get a Lunar Guildsman in Nexus selling slaves to Malfeas, or a Lunar Tribesman breaking up those same caravans. All of that's consistant with the Silver Pact. They're all the same people. They just don't have a narrative they're bound to.<br /> <br /> Lunars had infinite variety. They could be tricksters, or monsters, heroes or villains. They could stand for anything or anyone or they could tear down whatever part of the world offended them. And that's what I loved about them.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if this is negative. Trying not to start a flame war, but... 3E Lunars just depress me thus far.)</div> </div> </div> </div>3E doesn't actually look to be taking that away - not going by Masters of Jade, which was written with 3E in mind, and features Lunars who appear entirely unconcerned with any war against the Realm or Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:32:29-07:00","id":281370,"title":"","content":"The main problem with the Silver Pact and TSR is they were trying to port the Garou Nation (or the Ahabi, or the Beast Courts...same concept) into Creation. The Garou Nation and those other groups have specific purposes in OWoD and their constituent Tribes and customs reinforce and justify their existence. The goal of the Garou Nation is pretty clear: prevent the Apocalypse. It's straightforward, it's fundamental to the nature of werewolf society, it's easy to use and implement and create intra-group drama for because of unique Tribal identity and history. That purpose and those constituent entities do not transplant well into Creation and a society of only a few hundred Lunars which should, logically, be spread across the face of the world. That and how most of the Silver Pact's constituent groups made no sense for why they would be separate entities within the umbrella...<br /> <br /> The TSR may have had some potential but it just never made sense why the Lunars <i>as a whole</i> chose to do that, and there was no viable long-term plan for the 2e TSR. It was basically &quot;hey everyone do your own thing.&quot; I much prefer 3e's concept of maybe creating or guiding a culture to weaponize it against the Realm, with the goal of deploying several such cultures against Realm holdings simultaneously across Creation, but then again the 3e concept of a more unified Lunar culture makes a lot more sense than the Silver Pact or 2e TSR ever did. Like, TSR-esque projects are perfectly in theme for some Lunars, and would be pretty different depending on what cultural value they wanted to emphasize, but by making it a universal thing that all Lunars do just made no sense (kind of like the 2e concept of Lunars = Stewards to begin with).<br /> <br /> So, like...to me it's just a huge morass that I won't miss it. 2e did this thing where it painted splats with way-too-broad brushes at a baseline and later books built on that to destroy any sense of nuance. Basically everyone but the Solars and Alchemicals suffered from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:48:51-07:00","id":281387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281218#post281218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thousand Streams River has been confirmed as not coming back in 3e (in fact, it was confirmed as axed back in 2e, as in &quot;will never be mentioned again.&quot;)<br /> <br /> So can everyone else. &quot;Lunars NUMBAH ONE&quot; was never a workable concept; all of the Exalted are badass and dangerous fighters in their own way.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's really sucks. I mean, what they will do in Creation? They need some idea.<br /> But Lunars have a chance in one-to-one fight against abyssals. In exalted &quot;werewolves&quot; aren't forder for &quot;vampires&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 10-14-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:57:31-07:00","id":281389,"title":"","content":"I second a lot of these things, but I must admit, one of the things that appeal to me was the Solar-Lunar bond. The mechanic was solid meh, until the Solars got all the mind-rape charms and it became da fuck, and even before that there was the in-setting explanation that was just so much &quot;what.&quot;<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Lunars as stewards, that they mimic their patron by choosing someone or something - a person, a group, a culture, a place, a concept - to dedicate themselves to. I love them as wandering heroes, freely walking the world in search of something worthy of their interest - and maybe, protection and even service. I love them as behind-the-scenes masterminds doing weird stuff working towards their own obscure goals. I love them as legendary monsters, as well as those who hunt them.<br /> <br /> I just love them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T12:59:37-07:00","id":281394,"title":"","content":"The real problem with the TSM was that it was a retcon, and a fairly obvious one. &quot;Oh, all these places were created by Lunars.&quot; would have worked if it had been with new areas of the setting, maybe in all those big blank spaces in the corners of the map. But instead, it was with places that plainly hadn't been created with that intent, and it added nothing new to them. It looks like 3E will be doing a better take on the same idea with the Lunar dominions, which going by the map, seem to be mostly new places designed from the ground up.<br /> <br /> One thing I like is the theme of Lunars being unbreakable. They lost their purpose, they were thrown into an environment that tried to unmake everything they were, infested with infinite creatures of madness, and the most powerful empire in the world has been trying for centuries to exterminate them. <i>And it wasn't enough.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:02:17-07:00","id":281397,"title":"","content":"@marin: Eh. Exceptions to every rule. Before individuality was the default for Lunars, and I liked it. Now... well, we haven't seen the finished work yet, but I'm not hopeful. And here's a passage from Masters of Jade that I feel underlines my fears about the Realm War becoming the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lunars carry on as remnants of a fallen era. They are a living history, chained to a world they despise, and yet one they must save if any semblance of their memory is to continue on with any kind of meaning. For the Lunar Exalted, existence is a matter of extremes. They could allow the world to be swallowed by the Wyld, and then they would have nothing left on which to write their tale of sorrow, and no one left to hear it. While some would find comfort in such an end, the Lunars rage against it. After all, Luna chose them to be the ultimate survivors.<br /> <br /> So, as they strike out against a world whose destiny they have deemed illegitimate and false\u2014as they flense the world of progress and fight to drive it back into the darkness of the Fallen Age\u2014they also fight to protect Creation and her peoples. They are there to punish, but also to preserve. The world cannot know what it has lost until it becomes aware of that loss. To do that, it must survive. </div> </div> </div>@Zelbinnean: Correct me if I'm wrong, but did 2E ever say that every Lunar acted towards the TSR? The Winding Path did, because that was kinda their purpose as a group, and select others did (those who wanted to basically), but most of the other groups had their own priorities. Some Lunars started their own societies.... but I never remember a bit saying everyone had to or that it was obligatory. Just that it was a commonly agreed upon group philosophy<br /> <br /> (Also, I don't know OWoD, and like Lunars as Stewards <i>and </i>feel that their internal groups in 2E made sense... but all of that's just matters of opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:10:13-07:00","id":281402,"title":"","content":"Well, there were a bunch of reasons they called my attention at first.<br /> <br /> First, the silver motif caught my eye. Yes, a bit shallow, but gold is super tacky while silver tends to look much better on everything :P<br /> <br /> Then there is the TSR. I actually liked the idea of people trying to make it so that societies didn't need Exalted for basic every day survival. It seemed smart and actually rather constructive.<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that they aren't LOOK AT ME I'M SO AWESOME READ AS THE ENTIRE SETTING REVOLVES AROUND ME like the Solars were. They're strong (theorethically) without being THE most powerful actors in the setting assumed to eventually triumph at anything given enough time like Solaroids felt. That struck a nice balance in my scale of interests.<br /> <br /> I liked the whole intimacy focus idea that people posited, too. See, here's a thing. Exalted enshrines ambition, wanting to be the very best like no one ever was, having great huge ambitions to change the world in your image, living for great big ideals good or bad, all that jazz. These are <i>really </i>hard for me to get into. I can do it, but it's a definite roleplaying challenge. If I was given the world in a platter I'd trade it in for a little home at the mountain with a good internet connection and close to my family. But Exalting because you simply <i>refuse</i> to go down no matter how much shit the universe drops on you, I can get that. Dedicating yourself to <i>people</i>, and to protecting that which you love, I can <i>get </i>that. That is satisfying to me. I leave being the king of the pirates or whatever for whoever wants it.<br /> <br /> On that note, I LIKE being support. I like seeing others succeed thanks to me practically more than I like succeeding myself. I don't mind being the backbone that gets no face time.<br /> <br /> And on the note of the Exaltation, the whole perseverance thing. I like the heroes who go on and on and on even as they bleed and die, refusing to fall down until they fulfill their purpose.<br /> <br /> Then there was the whole illusionary and fluidity motif, the whole stalker in the night business. I am a wellknown player of illusionists and other such types, and so the Lunars sounded great. Then, of course, I discovered that the Lunars had almost fuck all for proper illusions, which made me sad and annoyed.<br /> <br /> Probably a handful of things more.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yeah, on the 3rd Edition Lunars comments... the dev comments and Masters of Jade notes have made my group basically expect them to be a villain splat for them, so, you know, I expect I'll probably be playing less Lunars in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 10-14-2014, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:18:50-07:00","id":281410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280913#post280913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody like Lunars? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know I don't,<br /> <br /> 1st Ed: Werewolf: The Beginning. I like W:tA. As a prequel to W:tA, 1st Ed Lunars are great. As Exalted, they're restricted to &quot;NPC Barbarians only&quot; turf. They are too narrowly pegged, and built as antagonists to showcase how much Solars rule.<br /> <br /> 2nd Ed: Lunars are now Silver Solars. Which is to say, Solars that suck. &quot;Anything you can't do, I can do better. Anything I can do, you could do better.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281041#post281041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it might be an unpopular view of them, one of my favorite things about lunars is their total lack &quot;to do lists&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I can (apathetically) agree with this. (And God_of_Awesome).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:23:00-07:00","id":281415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280918#post280918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow I'd forgotten that was a thing that happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enlightened Whale And Flowerpot Technique!<br /> <br /> But yeah, for me, the two big selling points of Lunars have always been shapeshifting, in both the turn-into-X and the impromptu-flesh-sculpted-tools senses, and the Thousand Streams River, which struck me as one of the few truly <i>constructive</i> setting-encouraged courses available to <i>any</i> splat.<br /> <br /> I'll wait and see how what we get in 3E instead of these turns out before I make any judgements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:43:35-07:00","id":281422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281337#post281337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars had existed... largely apart from Creation and the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Creation is <i>the setting of the game</i>, this is a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:52:02-07:00","id":281426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281422#post281422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Creation is <i>the setting of the game</i>, this is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not... really? It's not like a Lunar has no personal ties to Creation. Just that they didn't have a unified thesis statement. Does the splat as a whole need some specific universal tie to Creation?<br /> <br /> A Lunar fighting the Realm was still perfectly possible. But he didn't need to fight the Realm because he was a Lunar. That wasn't a default. If he fought the Realm that was because of his personal beliefs slash background, rather than because of their Exaltation type.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more a weakness of the other splats, most of them are wedded to a specific narrative, to a greater or lesser degree (the biggest exception being DBs IMO, who I also like.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:00:50-07:00","id":281430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281422#post281422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Creation is <i>the setting of the game</i>, this is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can't destroy Creation! That's where I keep my STUFF!<br /> <br /> - The Tick. (Paraphrasing a bit, but pretty much.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:21:01-07:00","id":281443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281426#post281426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's more a weakness of the other splats, most of them are wedded to a specific narrative, to a greater or lesser degree (the biggest exception being DBs IMO, who I also like.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars don't, though (&quot;returning God-Kings who will either save the world or destroy it&quot; is not very specific compared to the themes of Sidereals, most Abyssals, GSPs, and most DBs). Largely because there is no mostly-unified Solar organization in the Second Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:38:10-07:00","id":281485,"title":"","content":"Eh. Personal judgement. God Kings, opposition by the Wyld Hunt, having to deal with the world that's forgotten them... all these things aren't in every Solar chronicle, but are very much the default. It's not as inviolate as Sidereals (All servants of heaven) Abyssals/GSPs (Who either embrace their progenitor's plans or oppose them) but it's very much a base narrative that some people build away from.<br /> <br /> None of these are universal, of course, but they're encouraged. And Lunars didn't have something like that, which I appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:38:59-07:00","id":281489,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Lunars... vaguely romantic Lunar-y shaped notions (or phrases) which appeal to me are -<br /> <br /> Being able to choose your body.<br /> <br /> Being at one with nature.<br /> <br /> (and getting strength from that, in a deeper and more complete sense than mere Survival Charms offer you).<br /> <br /> Endure. Survive. Adapt. Outlast. Win.<br /> <br /> Oh the night is my world... In the day, nothing matters. In the night, no control. I live among the creatures of the night (tldr; Lunars feel like they belong to the world of the night, in a way the other Exalts really feel like they belong to the day, even if they're Night, if you get my meaning).<br /> <br /> Animal senses.<br /> <br /> Having a mind which is faster, more enduring, more focused than the human in a way that is not the same as turning skill and knowledge up to 11.<br /> <br /> Not being urbane, and if you are urban, you are something else which is intrusive, colonising and thriving there, playing &quot;their&quot; game better than &quot;they&quot; play it, wrong but right.<br /> <br /> I like that the Lunars feel they have a kind of sense of brotherhood to them, that's more a fellowship than the Solars get, as a splat, which is not like the bureaucratic fellowship of the Sidereals or the blood ties and national bonds of the Dragonbloods. I like that this brotherhood has an natural animal like feel to it, a bloodied feel, beyond the artificiality and falseness of human society and its ideologies and convention. (At the same time, there is animal cunning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:56:20-07:00","id":281506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281485#post281485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of these are universal, of course, but they're encouraged. And Lunars didn't have something like that, which I appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I feel like that causes its own problems, with a lack of splat-specific general/default thematics (hence why we got crappy barbarians and then Silver Solars). The agenda helps with that, but too much of an agenda can overly constrain the types of stories for the splat (see: Abyssals). It's a really delicate balance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:26:50-07:00","id":281516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281387#post281387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's really sucks. I mean, what they will do in Creation? They need some idea.<br /> But Lunars have a chance in one-to-one fight against abyssals. In exalted &quot;werewolves&quot; aren't forder for &quot;vampires&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, like I said, it's not that Lunars <i>won't</i> sometimes influence nations from behind the scenes over generations as part of a social engineering thing. It's just no longer going to be their big thing. From what we've been told, there will be a lot more focus on Lunars as outsiders waging a guerilla (or gorilla) war against the Realm, but I suspect that there will be a lot of other stuff, too. Most simply, like some people have said above, Lunars are generally more scattered and disorganized than most of Creation's Exalted (bar Solars), which puts them in a weaker position in some respects but also leaves players and writers a lot more options with what to do with them.<br /> <br /> And Lunars are one of the more fight-y Exalted, sure, but it makes me leery to have people say that what they like about them is how they kick ass, because... Sidereals are also fight-y Exalted. And so are DBs and Abyssals and Infernals and Solars and Alchemicals and, probably, Liminals and Getimans and so on. They fight in different ways, but &quot;combat&quot; is a bit broad for anyone to universally be the best at it -- people excel in specific <i>types</i> of combat (in the sense that Solars excel at talented swordsmanship and Sidereals are hidden masters who expose their true power at end of their elaborate plans, etc.)<br /> <br /> One of the problems Lunars have had in the past is that their books have often had this chest-beating about how Lunars are THE BEST and MORE THAN A MATCH FOR ANYONE, beyond what you see anywhere else (even Solars, despite having a theme of raw power, are generally fairly low-key about making comparisons to other Exalted, really.) And this has caused problems, because Lunar mechanics can't really give them the kind of &quot;fuck the other Exalted, LUNAR&quot; combat prowess that some parts of their books implied they had. I mean, Lunars are awesome, but more than anyone else their writing sometimes seemed intended to encourage dick-measuring, which slammed headlong into the fact that other Exalted are awesome, too, and better at certain types of fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-14-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:49:06-07:00","id":281540,"title":"","content":"Absolutely not trolling at all, before anyone says anything, but I really like Lunars because they provide a very interesting source of NPCs for Solar games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T16:21:27-07:00","id":281597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he didn't need to fight the Realm because he was a Lunar. That wasn't a default. If he fought the Realm that was because of his personal beliefs slash background, rather than because of their Exaltation type.</div> </div> </div> </div> Lunars in Third Edition will widely oppose the Realm on account of being Lunars, but that means something more complicated than &quot;Lunar Exaltation automatically carries a hostility towards the Realm in it&quot; or &quot;all Lunars are instantly loyal to the nebulous concept of Lunarness&quot;. It includes factors like &quot;the Realm will religiously hunt you down and destroy you on account of being a Lunar regardless of anything else you do&quot;. I imagine the Silver Pact will be akin to, say, everybody who was ever aligned in opposition against Napoleon Bonaparte (there were literally radical liberal reformists alongside the worst kinds of conservative aristocrats in Russia alone when it came to the opinion and material support of &quot;Napoleon needs to go down&quot;); the Realm are the ones creating the category umbrella for their enemies to neatly fall into line within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T16:39:53-07:00","id":281614,"title":"","content":"If anything, I imagine that part of the premise of the Caul and the Black Lion and tithes sent thereof is that it provides a means for Lunars who want to be personally less involved in fighting the Realm a way out; support the efforts to pin down Faxai, and you're creating a key strategic zone to which the Realm will send resources that can't then be used to destroy you or your works while you go about doing whatever else it is you want. Or a line of alliance to any other Lunars more focused on fighting the Realm; the point is to have some kind of buffer zone against the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T20:48:18-07:00","id":281886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281238#post281238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get how this is a Lunar-specific game theme. Any splat could do this; it's more of a general game premise and storytelling model than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly IS a Lunar-specific game theme?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T21:42:29-07:00","id":281923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281886#post281886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly IS a Lunar-specific game theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head....<br /> <br /> 1. Shape shifting into a feline and chasing a ball of yarn.<br /> 2. Exalted version of Furries (yiffing included)<br /> 3. Arguing that Beast Boy should lead the Teen Titans rather than Robin<br /> 4. Seeing exactly how many bestiality and phytophiliac concepts they can fit into a game before people need to use google to understand what they are talking about.<br /> 5. Once everyone has used google, present a historical or mythological examples in an faux-educated manner to belittle those who get squeamish about such things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T21:53:40-07:00","id":281931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281886#post281886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly IS a Lunar-specific game theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have lacked any coherent splat themes beyond &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and without a coherent splat theme it's impossible to really provide an overarching default game theme for an all-Lunar game. I mean, aside from &quot;raiding barbarians&quot; which is kind of a crap default and too narrow for a whole splat (but it's what we got in 1e lol). I don't even think 3e's &quot;Caul insurgency&quot; motif is going to be as all-pervasive as the default game themes for Sidereals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, or Dragon-Bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-15-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:11:58-07:00","id":281941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281886#post281886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly IS a Lunar-specific game theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Madam Satrap, there's someone here to see you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I thought I told you to send everyone away for the night.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I did, but she killed me and took my shape.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:12:32-07:00","id":281942,"title":"","content":"Freedom.<br /> <br /> Lunars are ideally suited towards being completely alone with no equipment then going anywhere and flourishing. Their freedom extends past being simply self-sufficient and into the realm of altering their own shape and identity. The only thing that limits a Lunar is them self, usually because they have formed an emotional attachment to another. But, I feel that Lunars can free themselves from even those bonds, though not without pain. Freedom has a cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4029-isvarg","name":"Isvarg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4029_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:15:18-07:00","id":281945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281941#post281941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Madam Satrap, there's someone here to see you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I thought I told you to send everyone away for the night.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I did, but she killed me and took my shape.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a good trick, but I wouldn't say you could run a game around just repeating that scene over and over with different participants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:24:05-07:00","id":281955,"title":"","content":"So some people laments the loss the TSS acting as a story narrative and homebase for Lunar, and some people likes how Lunar don't tie to anything and can do whatever they want. Lunar fan sure is a contradictory bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:33:27-07:00","id":281964,"title":"","content":"Even &quot;raiding barbarians&quot; isn't a very Lunar-specific game theme. Any Solar or outcaste DB who Exalts in the periphery of Creation can do that. (It is a bit different for DBs because they are not Anathema and would therefore have the option of turning their power into a different way of life; but there's lots of reasons why a DB barbarian might choose not to.)<br /> <br /> Ultimately, what Lunars offer in terms of their place in the setting is a chance to be similar to Solars (outcasts, Anathema, chosen from the great mass of humanity without warning) without being Solars. In fact, given the extreme similarities in terms of their position in the setting, it might be easier to list the things that make Lunars distinct from Solars:<br /> <br /> * Shapeshifting, obviously, as has been said.<br /> <br /> * Attribute-based charms. I feel that this is of dubious worth, because most things are Attribute + Ability, and even the things that aren't are often thematic to both splats; so if you rely on this, it mostly just means that you do the same things as Solars but with a slightly different arrangement. It does mean that the Lunar strategist / general caste is probably their thinky No Moons or talky Changing Moons whereas the Solar strategist caste is the fighty Dawns, among other things, which has some thematic implications; but I think that overall this can only offer minor flavor distinctions and that the game (and some fans) have leaned way too hard on it.<br /> <br /> * Lunars have been present for the past 1500 years. Again, this is of dubious worth. Players like to talk about the lack of Lunar integration into the setting and the fact that this mostly just gives you a bunch of (by game-design) necessity insane or useless elders. But I think that those are secondary to the underlying issue: Even if you have the Caul or whatever, even if you give Lunars a &quot;mark&quot; on the setting, without changing the nature of Lunars they're not going to get much of a unique overarching 'inheritance' from those 1500 years the way DBs have the Realm or Sidereals have the Bureau of Destiny. They can't, really. It doesn't work with the Solar random-Exalt-wherever Exaltation style or with any part of the setting as it stands. Sure, you can write in Lunar accomplishments, but you can't turn these accomplishments into a core part of the Lunar thematic (and into totally-unique Lunar stories) without drastically changing both Lunars and the setting.<br /> <br /> * Lunar charms have a vague and poorly-defined supernatural theme, including some sorts of den things and some illusions. You could develop this into something that makes them more clearly distinct, but I don't think you could develop it to the point where it completely defines their playstyle without fairly radically changing what Lunars are. (There have been projects to this end, of course.) It's a flavor, basically, but it doesn't give them a unique story as it stands.<br /> <br /> * Related to that, Lunars are less dependent on infrastructure, I guess...? The reason I'm dubious about this (even though it will apparently inform the backstory of 3e a lot more) is because infrastructure only plays a role in a few games to begin with and, since they're designed around this reality, none of the other splats are actually <i>that</i> dependent on infrastructure in the first place. You can wave your hand at this to explain certain things about the backstory, basically, but I don't think it's likely to define gameplay much.<br /> <br /> * Lunars are (or can be) paired with Solars, in one way or another. This has had its own problems, but it's worth mentioning because it turns one of their weaknesses (the fact that their position in the world and their Exaltation mechanics are largely a carbon-copy of Solars) into a potential strength (since that similarity then serves to strengthen the bond between Lunars and Solars.)<br /> <br /> * Lunars are somewhat less powerful than Solars, overall, and are not necessarily as central to this prophecy of Creation's doom. Woo. I'm noting this for the sake of completeness -- it theoretically enables some Lunar stories you couldn't tell with Solars -- but I don't think many people want this to be their defining feature. Aside from the fact that the distinction isn't overwhelming or anything, it doesn't really add much because the DBs and Sidereals seem to have decided long ago to treat Lunars as an existential threat to Creation regardless. Anyway, this has caused problems because, in light of the failures of the previous points, this and shapeshifting have often come to feel like Lunars' <i>only</i> real features.<br /> <br /> Obviously, my takeaway from that is that exploring and expanding on shapeshifting (making it more powerful and easy to use, and relying on it as much as possible for Lunar magic, though perhaps not exclusively) is probably the best way to make Lunars distinct. Even with that, though, I don't feel that Lunars will ever be as unique as DBs, Sidereals, Abyssals, or Infernals (and the only reason Solars aren't on that list is because they lose much of their uniqueness to Lunars, sharing their place as Anathema who, well, lack an inherent place in the world.)<br /> <br /> If I was designing the game from scratch (and felt a desire to keep Lunars in some form), I would probably change the fundamental mechanics of how the Lunar Exaltation operates and is passed down, replacing it with something that offers unique stories that can't be told with other kinds of Exalted. I doubt that 3e will do this, though, since it can't be done without invalidating existing Lunar concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-15-2014, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:47:41-07:00","id":281973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281964#post281964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was designing the game from scratch (and felt a desire to keep Lunars in some form), I would probably change the fundamental mechanics of how the Lunar Exaltation operates and is passed down, replacing it with something that offers unique stories that can't be told with other kinds of Exalted. I doubt that 3e will do this, though, since it can't be done without invalidating existing Lunar concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah for all that 3e is supposed to be a game line wholly separate from its predecessors, there doesn't seem to be much interest in or chance of burning down certain things that have existed since the beginning, for good or ill. Then again it's always easier to add wholly new stuff than to remove or completely replace longstanding stuff, since the grognards will only truly vocally freak out over the latter. I just don't particularly see the need to preserve badly-done concepts existing in what are effectively different game systems (with different mechanics) that happen to occupy the same fictional setting. But that's me.<br /> <br /> That said, Infernals are supposed to be <i>radically </i>changing in tone as well as mechanical implementation, as are Abyssals (at least in mechanics) and there haven't been huge cries against this yet (even lacking specific details on what the changes will be). The Caul and Lunar-Sidereal war does sound cool but I wonder if it'll push the envelope enough to give Lunars an actual complete set of themes. I don't know if it can, though - I'd think the themes would need to be there and the setting history rises up around them, not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T23:05:14-07:00","id":281980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281964#post281964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was designing the game from scratch (and felt a desire to keep Lunars in some form), I would probably change the fundamental mechanics of how the Lunar Exaltation operates and is passed down, replacing it with something that offers unique stories that can't be told with other kinds of Exalted. I doubt that 3e will do this, though, since it can't be done without invalidating existing Lunar concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden is on record as saying that Lunar players are going to have the most difficult time porting their Chosen into 3rd Edition. Take that as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T01:21:03-07:00","id":282047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281955#post281955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So some people laments the loss the TSS acting as a story narrative and homebase for Lunar, and some people likes how Lunar don't tie to anything and can do whatever they want. Lunar fan sure is a contradictory bunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes they are.<br /> On top of what you mentioned, there are also Lunar fans who hate the fact that Lunars are animal-themed. Whereas for others, that's the whole point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T03:00:54-07:00","id":282130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280913#post280913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody like Lunars? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gonna be honest and say that I don't really care for lunars. As the perpetual ST, lunars are a goddam pain to balance anything for. Also it annoys me (2e) that attributes cost less and abilities cost more for them, when attributes actually DO more and abilities do less for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:37:50-07:00","id":282160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281964#post281964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * Lunars have been present for the past 1500 years. Again, this is of dubious worth. Players like to talk about the lack of Lunar integration into the setting and the fact that this mostly just gives you a bunch of (by game-design) necessity insane or useless elders. But I think that those are secondary to the underlying issue: Even if you have the Caul or whatever, even if you give Lunars a &quot;mark&quot; on the setting, without changing the nature of Lunars they're not going to get much of a unique overarching 'inheritance' from those 1500 years the way DBs have the Realm or Sidereals have the Bureau of Destiny. They can't, really. It doesn't work with the Solar random-Exalt-wherever Exaltation style or with any part of the setting as it stands. Sure, you can write in Lunar accomplishments, but you can't turn these accomplishments into a core part of the Lunar thematic (and into totally-unique Lunar stories) without drastically changing both Lunars and the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that between the idea that Lunars have been consistently persecuted over that time, which means that even if you're a new Lunar and your personal exposure is limited, you kind of become drawn into a culture of it, and the notion that the nature of Lunars has changed in response to that context, it means more than you're giving it credit for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T06:45:28-07:00","id":282225,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of shapeshifting monster and/or trickster and/or sagely &quot;outsider&quot;-type heroes. That said, I don't feel that 2E lunars did a really great job of enabling you to play any of those, and there is nothing else at all that really appealed to me about the splat.<br /> <br /> I'm still disturbed by the heart-eating and the fandom-supported notions of beastmen army-breeding.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T06:53:59-07:00","id":282229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281980#post281980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden is on record as saying that Lunar players are going to have the most difficult time porting their Chosen into 3rd Edition. Take that as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take that as Lunars having much larger mechanical changes than most splats, which could very well imply radical changes to the themes that are expressed by their native mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T06:55:07-07:00","id":282231,"title":"","content":"All right, some other thoughts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=281964#post281964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even &quot;raiding barbarians&quot; isn't a very Lunar-specific game theme. Any Solar or outcaste DB who Exalts in the periphery of Creation can do that. (It is a bit different for DBs because they are not Anathema and would therefore have the option of turning their power into a different way of life; but there's lots of reasons why a DB barbarian might choose not to.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though there may be a measure of distinction there if &quot;Solar barbarians&quot; have a stronger tendency to come across as people from barbarian cultures who became Solars and then championed them, as opposed to Lunars who might have more of a sense of being people who live on the periphery because they were banished there and wait to use the already present peoples in their returns and revenges (a motif that might be able to carry through even when they're also Lunars who naturally originated out there). Maybe also some stylistic and mechanical flourishes to give a sense of Lunars really belonging in the wilderness, more than merely being able to get by out there (this is not the same thing as having every person who Exalts as a Lunar run away from cities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Attribute-based charms. I feel that this is of dubious worth, because most things are Attribute + Ability, and even the things that aren't are often thematic to both splats; so if you rely on this, it mostly just means that you do the same things as Solars but with a slightly different arrangement. It does mean that the Lunar strategist / general caste is probably their thinky No Moons or talky Changing Moons whereas the Solar strategist caste is the fighty Dawns, among other things, which has some thematic implications; but I think that overall this can only offer minor flavor distinctions and that the game (and some fans) have leaned way too hard on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd feel that, following the example of the Alchemicals, it would be better to define what the Charms do first and then the fact that they're bought with Attributes is a fairly minor thing after that, even if it still has implications for how much of your Charmset you can gain access to for any given stat purchase. Maybe also contribute to a sense of a different feel for what the Charms are and do; Solar Ability Charms are about applying your skills in increasingly powerful ways, and apparently feel like that, maybe Lunar Attribute Charms could feel like gradual expansive transformations of their bodies and minds.<br /> <br /> That's before getting into the sense that a lot of how different Exalted will feel different might come in whole sequences of things... I can imagine that, even without turning directly into something inhuman, it might be possible for Lunars to have incentives and results that feel like the fighting or other action style of a bestial lunatic. Maybe not as dramatic as Getimians with Charms that do different things depending on the motes you spend on them, but...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:38:55-07:00","id":282288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=282229#post282229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take that as Lunars having much larger mechanical changes than most splats, which could very well imply radical changes to the themes that are expressed by their native mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even just putting Charms and Knacks back together would cause substantial conversion issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:54:35-07:00","id":282298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=282288#post282288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even just putting Charms and Knacks back together would cause substantial conversion issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It's a largely semantic difference now, aside from say having a Perception-based shapeshifting thing be a prereq for a Stamina-based one...which would be problematic if moved back into Charms (1e charmcloud anyone?) But to me that particular problem is not a hard rejigger. I'd like to see some of the current-Knacks dropped and folded in to baseline shapeshifting/Sacred Hunt functionality, truth be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:38:25-07:00","id":282392,"title":"","content":"Speculation on ways for Lunars to be different from other Exalted in general, and Solars in particular:<br /> <br /> So, Lunars will probably be Attribute Exalted, meaning they won't have Sail Charms. Like, from the outset, the fact that Sail isn't going to be a prerequisite for any of their Charms means you don't have to figure out a Lunar way of sailing, but even beyond that I'd say that the image of &quot;be a good sailor&quot; won't be covered by any Lunar Charms, the way it is for Solars and Abyssals and even Dragon Blooded. We've seen, what, three Solar Sail Charms? And they're all about things like keeping yourself steady on a ship, or piloting it, or commanding its crew (along with some related incidentals)? I don't think Lunars will have any Charms like that.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that Lunars won't have some Charms that can be applied towards helping out in the tasks needed to use a ship; at the very least, if they can apply their Attribute in successes towards relevant dice rolls, well, you can very well have Lunars who have never set foot on a ship before being as good as some veteran mortal sailors, with some exertion. That on its own might cover the desire for versatility to be part of the Lunar bailiwick.<br /> <br /> That they're Attribute Exalted is a convenient way of facilitating this, but it's mostly just that when I imagine the broad outline of a Lunar, I don't see somebody that it makes sense for being notably good at conducting a ship. It's the same as that time I said that a Lunar warform didn't look like the kind of thing that should be distinguished by their weapon fighting.<br /> <br /> So what do I think a Lunar should do in a theater out to sea?<br /> <br /> Well, from the outset, they may very well be able to shapeshift into a marine animal (or a bird, if that's more helpful), something extremely easy to acquire and cheap to perform, and that on its own means you'll be able to go about at sea better than many Exalted. Even a Solar with relevant Sail and Athletics Charms... I can see them as being able to not drown, and even be extremely powerful swimmers, but still people who move in water in the manner of a human. Like, you'll be a very good swimmer, but being in the water still means you're largely confined to swim actions, I think. Various marine animals manage to neatly combine swimming with a few other things.<br /> <br /> But even a Lunar who isn't shapeshifting into marine life... I can see them as having Strength and Stamina Charms that make them extremely powerful swimmers, maybe even faster and more maneuverable than Solars (even if Solars have a competitive spirit that lets them keep up with and overtake faster swimmers). I can imagine Lunars zooming about like torpedos in their human body, which includes having the force to rend the hulls of ships apart with relative ease, possibly even easier than Solars would. A Solar out to sea is probably using Sail Charms, in which case using that incredible Lunar strength to take the extremely vital ship out from under him is going to put a damper on his day. So that's a way to imagine how something tangible and relevant can be expressed in the idea of Lunars being less reliant on infrastructure, as well as how the Lunar image might make them better at some things than Solars.<br /> <br /> But Solars are still the more powerful Exalted, for reasons including the fact that they've got Sail Charms; an entire area of experise to which the Lunar Essence has basically no access whatsoever. One that can also somewhat cover using ships to resist and slay the kind of mythic sea monster that is the basis image of the strength and speed of the Lunar in water; Moby Dick doesn't need a ship, and when he destroys it the best the sailors can generally hope for is to drift to safety, but a sufficiently legendary ship, and its captain, can take down Moby Dick.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to Second Edition, where, if sailing had been a thing anybody cared about, they'd have designated an Attribute that would probably go with it a lot, and then make a subsection of &quot;sailing Charms&quot; under it, and fill it with weaker Solar Charms with a shallow Lunar skin. That arrangement of what Attribute Charms meant is why the relationship between Solars and Lunars never really expressed that idea Holden put forward, where Solars are the most powerful because there's not a thing they're comprehensively not good at.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I have an idea about how the new Edition might fulfill Jenna Moran's vision of how Sidereal Charms expressed the outline she was given better than even First Edition is, namely by placing the value on Abilities with <i>multiple paths</i> of competence, rather than custom Charms; the thing about Sidereal Charms wasn't just that they were the only ones you got, but that they all followed more-or-less single paths. From what we've seen and been told of Solar Charm cascades and purchasing, a lot will be defined in Solars taking different paths through their Abilities, and will hardly ever be able to snatch up everything. So that's something.<br /> <br /> I also think that, with what they've described of the combat system and the tactical profiles of the attack Abilities and Dodge and Resistance, not only does it seem more likely that there'll be a way to give different ways of fighting a more tangibly distinct feel, but I also think it might give a straightforward idea of how to grasp differences in Solar and Lunar fighting. Like, core Melee will apparently be &quot;has great defense and attacking up close, it builds momentum really well, it has a couple of ranged attack options&quot;; I imagine that a Solar weapon fighter will laregly have Charms based around expanding on that tactical parameter, while a Lunar weapon fighter will be relying on its core principles for their actual attack actions, underlined by the Lunar enhancement of the body that is pulling off those attacks, and around which is built a solid set of tactically useful Lunar shenanigans, that aren't so much about enhancing weapon fighting as synergizing with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:38:50-07:00","id":282456,"title":"","content":"From what I know about Lunars, I would say that it's their endless adaptability and indomitably that appeal to me the most - in theory, I have no idea how it's worked out in practice. Their world crumbled around them, their mates were slain, the rest of the Exalted Host turned on them and chose to hunt them down without mercy, driving them to the ends of the world... but they've survived and adapted - beaten but unbroken, making their tormentors pay dearly for each of their transgressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:57:14-07:00","id":284246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=282298#post282298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. It's a largely semantic difference now, aside from say having a Perception-based shapeshifting thing be a prereq for a Stamina-based one...which would be problematic if moved back into Charms (1e charmcloud anyone?) But to me that particular problem is not a hard rejigger. I'd like to see some of the current-Knacks dropped and folded in to baseline shapeshifting/Sacred Hunt functionality, truth be told.</div> </div> </div> </div>And was there any reason for them to be separate other than to mark Knacks as off-limits for Eclipses?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:30:12-07:00","id":284284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=284246#post284246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And was there any reason for them to be separate other than to mark Knacks as off-limits for Eclipses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally no.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eclipses can (and should!) be able to learn everything called a Charm that is printed. But Lunar shapeshifting is something they shouldn't be able to learn! And Lunars shouldn't have all shapeshifting functionality as a default, they should have to buy Charm-like effects to improve it. So...I'll make them not-Charms by calling them something else!&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously that is how it went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T17:24:16-07:00","id":284358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=284284#post284284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally no.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eclipses can (and should!) be able to learn everything called a Charm that is printed. But Lunar shapeshifting is something they shouldn't be able to learn! And Lunars shouldn't have all shapeshifting functionality as a default, they should have to buy Charm-like effects to improve it. So...I'll make them not-Charms by calling them something else!&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously that is how it went.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The reasons are that, as far as I can tell, yes. There are some other differences that grew out of that, and complement that, such as xp costs and training times being different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:57:38-07:00","id":285502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=284358#post284358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reasons are that, as far as I can tell, yes. There are some other differences that grew out of that, and complement that, such as xp costs and training times being different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is just annoying. Doubly so because it robbed the Lunars of tons of the most thematic Charm space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:06:08-07:00","id":290537,"title":"","content":"Well, I posted in the other one on Dragonbloods, so I might as well do a similar list here. Reasons I love Lunars:<br /> <br /> 1. You have a closer relationship to your deity than anybody else. Luna shows up, in person, at your Exaltation. You've MET your patron, which most other Exalts can't actually say, and which really helps give you a sense of the sacred to justify whatever your goals are.<br /> <br /> 2. Oh, man, do I love shapeshifting. Turning into a bird to scout out an enemy encampment from above, turning into a fish to travel downriver, turning into a mouse to sneak into a bank vault or a mammoth to charge an enemy army, it's just really satisfying to me to use forms to accomplish things I can't as a human. I love flying and swimming and burrowing best: new forms of locomotion delight me!<br /> <br /> 3. Hunting new shapes. When the ST describes some terrifying monstrosity, other PCs are like, &quot;crap, how do we kill it.&quot; Lunar PCs get to go &quot;I wanna EAT IT and TAKE ITS SKIN!&quot; Perhaps it just appeals to the part of me that loves Pokemon games, but eating a new creature and gaining a new form is WAY more exciting and satisfying to me than uncovering a cool new artifact or learning a new spell. It's so much fun!<br /> <br /> 4. Disguise! I enjoy doing the play-within-a-play thing and pretending to be a character who is herself pretending to be a character. Disguise makes for fun roleplaying, and the majority of Lunars engage in it at one time or another. You're always hiding from the Wyld Hunt by pretending to be a peasant in the Realm or sneaking into fancy parties by looking like the host's daughter or assassinating gods by posing as their virgin sacrifice or seducing Guild Factors in the form of their favorite concubine or pretending to be the family dog to get close the kid you think is getting abused...every Lunar has disguise built right into them, and since I love disguises I love Lunars.<br /> <br /> 5. Talking to animals. No, seriously. Dog-tongue method is like, my favorite Lunar charm. Nothing makes the setting feel as wonderfully mythic as getting advice by talking to animals. Gods are neat and all, but getting relationship advice from a fox or asking a squid if there's any sunken ships in the area is really fun for me! I love it even more when I'm STing, because I love running talking animals. They're not people-smart, and their personalities are just a little alien (or sometimes very alien, for weirder creatures), so I love running them as NPCs for the same reason I love running demons: it's fun to get into an unfamiliar mindset. Animal NPCs are often beloved by PCs and can quickly become Familiars or recurring friendlies, and I enjoy the Lunars-befriending-animals thing that tends to happen in any game where a Lunar talks to critters.<br /> <br /> 6. Ruling in Wyld Places. I love that Lunars are at home in the wild places of Creation, because those places are gorgeous and full of fun adventures! Deep black forests, steaming jungles, towering waterfalls, echoing mountain caverns, the crushing depths of the ocean, the canopy of a mile-high tree, the burning sands of the South, the ice-floes and floating islands of the North...Lunars can easily get to and thrive in these places, and in my experience they tend to get used more often when there's a Lunar in the party. The edges of Creation are where the weird cool magic stuff happens, and I love floating palaces and rivers that run up into the sky and caverns made of tree roots and stuff. I love setting up homes there and building communities that survive in hostile or alien climes. I'm not a huge fan of the Silver Pact, but Lunars are superlatively talented magical humans, and it makes sense for them to desire human companionship and end up ruling groups of humans around them, and I love designing the strange societies Lunars can found and protect on the mad edges of the world.<br /> <br /> 7. The Solar Mate Thing. I'm not a fan of its 2E mechanical implementation, but I love the plotlines enabled by the idea of a Fated Soulmate. Love-that-transcends-lifetimes, eternal brofists, rivalry, undying hatred spanning the centuries, fear of a long-dead abuser, being twins and exalting at the same time literally EVERY time for two thousand years, taking turns killing each other since the First Age...so many fun plots come out of the Fated Soulmate thing. All Celestial Exalts get to play with the Past Lives shenanigans, but it's always been a big part of my Lunar games. The returning Solars are a big deal to everyone else because of their power, but to Lunars they're a big deal less because of their huge historic impact on world power centers and more because, dammit, my old flame is back in town and I'm not sure if we're going to make up or kill each other. The best stories are personal.<br /> <br /> 8. The Wyld Hunt: Solars and Lunars both get to deal with the Hunt...but the Hunt has predominantly been about hunting and killing newly exalted Lunars for centuries, and there's bad blood there. I love Lunar PCs who have recurring nightmares about getting murdered by the Hunt over and over and over in previous lives in different ways. I love Lunar stories where a group of PCs races to get to a newly exalted Lunar before the Hunt finds him. I love Lunar stories where the Wyld Hunt becomes the Hunted, and the Lunars slowly while away a Hunt too strong for them to directly overpower through subterfuge and guile. I love games of cat-and-mouse-and-Tyrant Lizard. I love playing a Lunar PC who pretends to be an Immaculate Monk and joins a Wyld Hunt to get their help finding his Solar mate or a monster they both want to take out. I love ambushing the Hunt with an army of barbarians, or getting ambushed myself. Solars can do all this...but again, the best stories are personal, and Lunars tend to have a more personal relationship with the ones hunting them.<br /> <br /> 9. Threatening to eat people. Seriously, everybody can be threatening, but if you're a Lunar and a local god is giving you guff, you can just politely mention that you love their new hairstyle, they're looking positively <i>delicious </i>today, and everybody involved knows you're pointing out that killing and eating him would be both doable and beneficial for you. It's small and it's silly, but most other Exalt types just don't get to threaten to eat people! Threatening to kill people works just fine, but there's something special about eating somebody, y'know?<br /> <br /> 10. Carrying other party members. My games are usually mixed games, and I love telling people to climb on my shoulders then dashing off as a mammoth or swooping down and picking up another PC as a giant eagle. Carrying other PCs is really satisfying for me!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:05:08-07:00","id":290808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=290537#post290537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. Threatening to eat people. Seriously, everybody can be threatening, but if you're a Lunar and a local god is giving you guff, you can just politely mention that you love their new hairstyle, they're looking positively <i>delicious </i>today, and everybody involved knows you're pointing out that killing and eating him would be both doable and beneficial for you. It's small and it's silly, but most other Exalt types just don't get to threaten to eat people! Threatening to kill people works just fine, but there's something special about eating somebody, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orichalcum Chef Style Solar works for this, too, and of course\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10. Carrying other party members. My games are usually mixed games\u2026 </div> </div> </div>In mixed games, it's usually the group's <i>Solar</i> who's carrying the party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:46:29-07:00","id":290823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=290808#post290808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum Chef Style Solar works for this, too, and of course\u2026<br /> <br /> In mixed games, it's usually the group's <i>Solar</i> who's carrying the party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I love Orichalcum Chef Style, but I've never actually had a chance to use it in a game. As for Solars carrying the party...I've never actually had that problem. Sure, the Solar kicks much ass at whatever their focus is, but in a mixed Celestial party everybody brings something to the table. And one of the things Lunars bring to the table is &quot;Get in my mouth! I'll turn into a whale and take a deep breath and swim you down to the subterranean manse at the bottom of the ocean!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T18:31:42-07:00","id":290930,"title":"","content":"I like the concept of what Lunars 'could&quot; be. The idea of the trickster, shapeshifter, shaman. I don't like what they've become, or were. I'm hoping 3rd time is the charm. But that and being a bit of a anthro fan helps, but eh. it's more a monster person thing I like too. And lunars are wicked monsters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T06:27:46-07:00","id":291257,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite things about the Lunars is the thematic purpose behind them, as can be seen by the personalities of their Patron...this is slightly inspired by a post I saw on an alternate interpretation of the Solar/Lunar Bond I have read.<br /> <br /> Solars: TUS is the absolute master of the direct approach. He doesn't really have to plan ahead, because he is just so freaking good that he curb stomps threats the moment they show up. His Chosen were built along the same philosophy. Masters of the direct approach. They attack, and it is like 'I punch you into the stratosphere.' They defend, and their response is basically 'lolno.' They do social combat, and it's functional mind-control. Heck, even stealth is generally 'I'm not actually hiding, I just edited myself out of your perception.' They solve all of their problems through raw, unbridled power. (The Infernals and Abyssals function in much the same way, as they are built off the same template)<br /> <br /> Sidereals: The Maidens cheat. That's the simple truth of dealing with them. The know what you are going to do before you do it, and have planned accordingly. For example, in the aftermath of the Primordial War, when the Underworld cropped up, isn't it so convenient that the Siddies already had charms for dealing with ghosts? Which had never existed before? Again, their Chosen are built along the same design...they cheat. A Siddie will tweak probability and causality to screw you over...and can generally be completely prepared for an opponent when they go up against them, and can always cheat their way out of a fight if they need to.<br /> <br /> But Luna...Luna is different. Conky and the Maidens were created to be exactly what they were (though who made the Maidens is still up for debate), Luna got there by fighting and clawing and murdering her way to the top of a pile of dead Othermoons, which he then ate. Discounting the Primordials (due to Geas), there have been extremely few instances that TUS couldn't just steamroll his opponents. Things aren't hard for him...he just does stuff, and it works. The Maidens cheat, they don't play fair. And they don't tend to get involved in fights that require them to play fair. Luna isn't Unconquerable, he doesn't have cheat codes to reality, so she does things the hard way. She can't just curb stomp all comers, she can't see threats before they arrive...so he has to be prepared for anything...has to adapt, has to change. As with the others, this carried over to the Lunars...they are the masters of asymmetrical warfare and adapting on the fly.<br /> <br /> That's why I like the Lunars. They, like Luna, do what needs to be done, because no one else can. If there's an enemy that can just be stomped, just call in a Solar, that's their specialty. If a threat can be foreseen, no need to call the Siddies, they already know and are working on it. But for that enemy that the Siddies don't see coming...that can cheap-shot a Solar...The Lunars will rip them to shreds...because Lunars, by their nature, are built to adapt to any threat. A great example of how this can work is in the Ink Monkey's bit on the Fair Folk...specifically &quot;Prince Laashe, the Morning Star.&quot; Laashe figures out kryptonite against Conky, and is outside fate so the Maidens don't see his plan coming. Laashe freaking wins. He is just about to take down TUS permanently, and make off with the godspear...when Luna cheap-shots him right out of existence.<br /> <br /> (Note: I don't think they were mechanically handled will in 2E, here's hoping that changes to bring them more in line with what I see)<br /> <br /> (Also, mixing gender pronouns when writing about Luna is fun!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T07:20:27-07:00","id":291320,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about ways that Holden's comment on rough Attribute magic compared to polished Ability magic might have some substance.<br /> <br /> On the face of it, I think I can gather something from previewed Solar Charms and Second Edition Alchemical Charms.<br /> <br /> The preview Solar Charms do seem to have a certain sense of being complex, or at least comprehensive; when they're not ones that explicitly do multiple things, they look like stuff that kind of gets into a certain process and fleshes out all the little widgets in it. They feel like rather procedural things, which I think lends itself to the characteristics the developers say they want to have Solar Charms to have. I can easily imagine that Terrestrial Charms will be similar, even if what they do is oriented towards a different motif and the actual effects might be generally weaker.<br /> <br /> When I think of Alchemical Charms, I get the general sense of them as being not so much things they can do as additions that have been bolted onto them that themselves do things. I think Alchemical Charms might tend to be fairly straightforward in that; they cover singular, straightforward effects (even if these can continually branch out in sub-modules), but this is aided by how they can get large, flexible suites of Charms, and how they can effectively dodge the concept of prerequisites while still referencing it.<br /> <br /> I imagine something broadly similar might go for Lunars. They won't get a Charm like Subject-Hailing Ideology, where it's fairly intricate in terms of how and why it affects people, and can potentially cover a wide range of situations, instead maybe something like a pheromone Charm that goes straight into brute-forcing certain kinds of Intimacy. But it could come from an Attribute that can cover a diverse number of Charms, and may itself be part of a cascade that snakes its way through several concepts, in a manner that covers them in a way distinct from the Alchemicals with their large number of Favoured Attributes and their Augmentations to boost stats and their cascades that pass through several different Attributes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, stuff that fells like having or using the Charm is a transformation to enable a straightforward effect in a manner similar to modular Alchemical additions.<br /> <br /> Also gives me a notion of how the shift in Lunar nature over time might be conveyed; the idea that having different needs means developing different Charms, which itself prompts a shift in one's outlook and even one's form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T10:25:09-07:00","id":291447,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I feel that a lot of the things that I love about Lunars has be already said: shapeshifting, animal and moon motifs, the mutative and wyld-manipulation effects, the broad scope of their charms. For me, the biggest reason of them is that they are instigators, agents of change, challengers of the status quo and guardians against stagnancy. Any exalt can cause change, but I feel Lunars have an intimate connection to it; they personify change. Their innate ability to infiltrate, to adapt, to alter what is and what isn't, and to deceive and inspire. The Moon's Chosen tap into chaos and apply it to Creation like a painter to a canvas.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The mechanics haven't always reflected this, but I feel the key tenet of the Lunar is to &quot;be the change&quot;. Don't let it be merely a byproduct of your actions, but to grok it. I hope we see more of this in future previews of the Lunars and the upcoming edition.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","user":"Binary Phantom","date":". 10-24-2014, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:44:42-07:00","id":291545,"title":"","content":"I imagine everything to like about Lunars can be summed up <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o0u4M6vppCI\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T15:18:02-07:00","id":291596,"title":"","content":"I actually liked Lunars years before I ever played my first game of Exalted. My friends described all the types of exalt to me, Solars seemed bland, Sidereals seemed strange and Dragonblooded seemed stuck up and weak. Lunars could be a gigantic ragebeast or a tiny fox-man ninja assassin, they got to turn into whatever animal they could hunt, and in addition their spirit totem which could be whatever and totally awesome.I liked how their attributes were easy to apply and how they got cool immunity to other people trying to shape them into things.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting was the biggest thing though, you spent barely any xp on it and it let you fly, breath under water, see in the dark, burrow through the ground, run faster, jump higher, sneak around, fight better, climb walls, spin webs, see better, hear better, enhanced senses of taste and smell, and a million other things. Then you spent some xp on it and it let you become immense or diminutive, become other people, plants even for god's sake!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:53:14-07:00","id":292733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=284284#post284284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally no.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eclipses can (and should!) be able to learn everything called a Charm that is printed. But Lunar shapeshifting is something they shouldn't be able to learn! And Lunars shouldn't have all shapeshifting functionality as a default, they should have to buy Charm-like effects to improve it. So...I'll make them not-Charms by calling them something else!&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously that is how it went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knacks also had a cloud structure, so there was a slightly different philosophy that went into them on that level. I can't suss out the design reasoning behind that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:03:36-07:00","id":292747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=292733#post292733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knacks also had a cloud structure, so there was a slightly different philosophy that went into them on that level. I can't suss out the design reasoning behind that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Charmcloud artifact? I don't hate the cloud structure of Knacks on a thematic level though. To me it can thematically make some sense. Mechanically, of course, it is a huuuuuge fucking mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T18:06:41-07:00","id":293329,"title":"","content":"I'm not a big fan of Lunars, I must admit. Maybe because in 2e they were pretty much the animal Exalted, and well, I'm not a big animal fan. Also, I find shapeshifting to be an uninteresting power in itself: it can be made interesting, but 2e Lunars didn't manage for me. I hope 3e will do something radical with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:18:23-07:00","id":293860,"title":"","content":"Here's one aside from the shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Lunars are Creation's first line of defense against the Wyld. They're the shield wall between reality and chaos. While the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded built themselves an empire, the Lunars were scouting out into the chaos to spy a Fae incursion coming straight for them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:12:19-07:00","id":294070,"title":"","content":"Lunars, no matter who or what they are, always have a kind of primal and visceral attraction to me. Also they are always very worldly and exotic. A stylistic degree of barbarism. They're also a bit of a character, as we personify certain animals with specific personality traits, and these traits carry over into Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:27:38-07:00","id":294194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=293860#post293860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one aside from the shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Lunars are Creation's first line of defense against the Wyld. They're the shield wall between reality and chaos. While the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded built themselves an empire, the Lunars were scouting out into the chaos to spy a Fae incursion coming straight for them</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the one thing they did in 2000 years as of 2e and nobody knows or really cares they did it. <br /> <br /> I'm over the trope of &quot;glorious heroism that is neither remembered nor recognized&quot; being applied to an entire splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:42:19-07:00","id":294218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294194#post294194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm over the trope of &quot;glorious heroism that is neither remembered nor recognized&quot; being applied to an entire splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But think of the poor Adamant Castes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:56:43-07:00","id":294230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294218#post294218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But think of the poor Adamant Castes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, optional Caste is optional. Much more narrow than a whole ~400-strong Creation-born Celestial splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:21:04-07:00","id":294292,"title":"","content":"I like them because they can be easily removed from the game without any consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T20:16:30-07:00","id":294478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294218#post294218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But think of the poor Adamant Castes!</div> </div> </div> </div>(Tastes soup of 1e and 2e)<br /> <br /> Needs less Super Secret Character seasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T20:41:11-07:00","id":294491,"title":"","content":"I liked them because they had so much hate and everyone was aching to make things up to fix them.<br /> <br /> And I was like, &quot;I like fixing things.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T22:38:33-07:00","id":294534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294218#post294218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But think of the poor Adamant Castes!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adamant Caste does and continues to do things and not get recognition for it. The Lunars <i>debatably</i> <b>contributed</b> to <i>one</i> thing almost a thousand years ago, and won't stop griping about it to everyone, to the point of literally declaring it an official faction in their useless society.<br /> <br /> (Debatable because no amount of scouting will defeat or prepare you for an army that stands without number, no amount of harrowing on the Lunars' part can meaningfully reduce their threat (and will always pale in comparison to the Empress shattering the entire army with a single shot), and the simple fact that the army of the Fair Folk literally had to be <i>invited in</i> means that if anything, the Lunars probably <i>underestimated</i> the raksha as a threat - after all, &quot;what's gonna happen, a First Age Solar walks across our boundaries and invites them in?&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea that &quot;You guys woulda been fucked if we hadn't interfered with the Fair Folk army&quot; <i>reeks</i> of sour grapes.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, there's still a lot I like about Lunars; them being &quot;Creation's first line of defense against the Wyld&quot; isn't one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-28-2014, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T04:16:54-07:00","id":294673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294218#post294218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But think of the poor Adamant Castes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd find their relationship with the Autochthonian spirit courts and patronage from the Divine Ministers and getting to live in glorious glittering cities amidst the wonders of the Elemental Pole of Crystal to go some ways towards making up the discrepancy. Even the inhabitants of the Adamant cities, depending on how many of them there are... I'm sure they're generally aware <i>that</i> their Champions are doing something worth honouring, even if they can never quite grasp what it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T14:55:41-07:00","id":295251,"title":"","content":"Well, I think I already answered this question earlier, but here's another reason.<br /> <br /> I like animals. I like dogs and cats and lizards and fish and hamsters and crows. I watch nature documentaries, and when I see a really neat animal, sometimes I am like: I want to Exalt THAT!. <br /> <br /> I want to play the archer fish Lunar with a pack (archer fish natural coordinate fire, and work together to ensure everyone gets to eat, even after the individual is full).<br /> I want to play the snake Lunar that challenges temples to fasting protests because I disagree with their religion and sit there for a month without moving, eating, or drinking (snakes do this).<br /> I want to play the octopus Lunar that rips off its own arm and throws it at you, allowing it to Clinch you and hold you in place while I go and deal with other things (also a real thing).<br /> I want to play the fungal Lunar that infects your brain and spreads through your entire village and controls your brain and forces you to build a tower for me (100% real. Well, 75%. Mostly).<br /> I want to play the hummingbird Lunar that sneaks into your camp and eats all of your supplies, because my metabolism is that high (technically they have a restricted diet, but whatever).<br /> I want to play the bird of paradise Lunar that is a professional dancer (go youtube this. Your life will be better).<br /> I want to play the armadillo lizard Lunar that grabs its own tail with its mouth and shows only spiky bits. This is real. Then I want to roll downhill at you at high speed. That is less real.<br /> I want to play the chameleon Lunar that uses its tongue to grab people's weapons and gear, perform grapples, or just poke people in the eyes.<br /> I want to play the frilled lizard Lunar so that I can be the world's most terrifying pacifist by mock charging while while looking to be five or six times my real size.<br /> I want to play the pistol shrimp Lunar so that when I punch you, it explodes with the heat and light of the surface of the sun, and works at range.<br /> I want to play the mimic octopus Lunar, so that I can shapeshift into anything I want, even when formlocked.<br /> <br /> I want to play a million more things, but that's a good list. Animals are awesome. Seriously, they are like WTF made into flesh and stuck in front of you to confuse the hell out of you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T16:41:43-07:00","id":295367,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs*<br /> <br /> They gave me TAW's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T18:27:30-07:00","id":296363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=280922#post280922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically I like playing something that's a bit otherworldly that stops short of being alien. Raksha are a bit too alien while Abyssals and Infernals both come with &quot;baggage&quot; that stop me from really making the most of that aspect of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>^Yes, this is my main thing with lunars, <br /> <br /> The other things I like, in a no real order...<br /> <br /> Moonsilver; I like the idea of a weapon that changes forms. I'm kind of hoping that evocations will let my daiklaive be Haru glory's Ten Commandments Sword.<br /> <br /> Not needing or warstrider to fight a giant monster, I can just join them in kaiju mode.<br /> <br /> I like DBT and mutation charms, as well as the &quot;tools from body&quot; bit. I like the idea of entering a specialized &quot;combat mode&quot;, as opposed to a &quot;social mode&quot; or &quot;stealth mode&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I like being able to create/hijack zombies without leaning necromancy, take that Abbysals.<br /> <br /> Things I like on a fluff level, but the crunch ruined it for me.<br /> <br /> SOLAR BOND; Just, solar bond. I'm sure you've already heard anything I could say on the topic.<br /> <br /> Tattoos/Tell; I really like the idea of these, but the implementation is a bit... Flawed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T12:55:26-07:00","id":297390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=294194#post294194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Literally the one thing they did in 2000 years as of 2e and nobody knows or really cares they did it.<br /> <br /> I'm over the trope of &quot;glorious heroism that is neither remembered nor recognized&quot; being applied to an entire splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was a good splat, i said the splay had a good idea IN it. And the idea that the Lunars are the first line of defense against the Fae is a GREAT idea - it gives the Lunars more range as characters, both collectively and individually. It gives them a primary threat to face at all times that isn't shared by all the other splats. It was something unique, something to latch onto and say 'This is what Lunars are for' rather than 'this is what Lunars do'.<br /> <br /> Solars are there to be paragons of perfection who decide how Creation will go from now on, they do this through powerful ability charms and high dice pools, and fight against the Wyld Hunt that is out to destroy them. Sidereals are there to manage fate, they do so by toying with the laws of reality, and their main enemies are bureaucracy and the fallen/dead primordials. (AFAIK). Abyssals are there to kill everything, they do so by manipulating death and the dead, and they fight against everything alive. Dragon Blooded are there to drown the enemy in numbers, they do this through teamwork, established infrastructure and the adoration of the public, and their main enemies are Anathema.<br /> <br /> Aside from Shield Wall against chaos, what are Lunars for?... To be the Solar's love interest/rival and the bitch to everyone else's butch. Yeah. How VERY compelling to play second fiddle to literally everyone. *sigh* They shapeshift, sure, but not to any central goal or idea, or to fight any particular enemy. They had the Thousand Streams River plan or whatever it was, but that wasn't compelling in the slightest because it was still about what OTHERS would do, not what the Lunars themselves were for.<br /> <br /> For every other detail of the 2e splat, all I could think about was how much of an inferiority complex this group had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:42:12-07:00","id":297455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297390#post297390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said it was a good splat, i said the splay had a good idea IN it. And the idea that the Lunars are the first line of defense against the Fae is a GREAT idea - it gives the Lunars more range as characters, both collectively and individually. It gives them a primary threat to face at all times that isn't shared by all the other splats. It was something unique, something to latch onto and say 'This is what Lunars are for' rather than 'this is what Lunars do'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fair Folk are far too broad, credible and interesting to solely be antagonists to the Lunars. They're not like Getimians will probably be.<br /> <br /> It also seems like the sort of thing that would actually make the Lunars really samey.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:35:48-07:00","id":297513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297455#post297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fair Folk are far too broad, credible and interesting to solely be antagonists to the Lunars. They're not like Getimians will probably be.<br /> <br /> It also seems like the sort of thing that would actually make the Lunars really samey.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're quite right, what about lovers and allies too? I actually found the idea that some Lunars lived so far in the edges of creation they're in the Middlemarches among the Fae quite interesting. I hope with the redevelopment of the Wyld I can have some awesome adventures in it, as flavourful as Malfeas and impassioned as the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T17:28:22-07:00","id":297636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297513#post297513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're quite right, what about lovers and allies too? I actually found the idea that some Lunars lived so far in the edges of creation they're in the Middlemarches among the Fae quite interesting. I hope with the redevelopment of the Wyld I can have some awesome adventures in it, as flavourful as Malfeas and impassioned as the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's become something of a gag in my circle's games that Lunars will inevitably have strange Fae allies. The two are similar enough and they seem to rub elbows enough that such alliances seem all but inevitable. Thus far, these have included a Catfish totem No Moon Lunar whose entire mission in life is to mock the Fae so as to prevent any one champion from repeating the Balorian Crusade. He's an amicable enough chap, but he finds ambitious Fae to be too silly to not rib, leaving to many Fae trying to find find his &quot;Weaknesses&quot; and follow him around. There was also a First Age Lunar Elder who self-stylized herself as a fairy princess, owning a small army of Fae vassals. She was amusing, being this Disney-esque princess, but treating her servants like dirt because &quot;They're not real people, you guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think that the Wyld can be a bit daunting to use, considering it's supposed to be the chaotic &quot;Other&quot;, but the times we've been there, our ST has used the Fae as a way to have a lot of fun with meta-humor, basically playing the &quot;Fae as Actors&quot; straight for humorous effect. This has given us a bit of normalcy what has been a lot of weirdness. Examples of this that we played through were a forest of pizza pruned by chef-gardeners and a Pokemon Safari Zone-esque Behemoth reserve, if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T00:03:00-07:00","id":297881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297455#post297455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fair Folk are far too broad, credible and interesting to solely be antagonists to the Lunars. They're not like Getimians will probably be.<br /> <br /> It also seems like the sort of thing that would actually make the Lunars really samey.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When did I say that the Fair Folk would solely be Lunar antagonists? When did I even imply that? &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> It might've been, except that you don't have to do JUST that. Creation has plenty of enemies to choose from. I just found it interesting - this was something the Lunars had that was unique to them. In addition, as you said yourself, the Fae are so broad and multifaceted that they can serve numerous roles as antagonists to the Lunars. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:01:33-07:00","id":297977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did I say that the Fair Folk would solely be Lunar antagonists? When did I even imply that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297390#post297390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the idea that the Lunars are the first line of defense against the Fae is a GREAT idea - it gives the Lunars more range as characters, both collectively and individually. <b>It gives them a primary threat to face at all times that isn't shared by all the other splats</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might've been, except that you don't have to do JUST that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the notion that all of them being &quot;the first line of defense against the Fae&quot; doesn't seem connected to the idea of &quot;giving them more range as characters&quot;.<br /> <br /> ... Wait...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">this was something the Lunars had that was unique to them</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm feeling something of a mixed message here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:36:13-07:00","id":298120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=297977#post297977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a fair bit of difference between 'Lunars are the only splat that has them as a primary threat woven into their history' (what i've been saying) and 'only Lunars ever fight them because otherwise Lunars suck' (what you seem to think I said) &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then the notion that all of them being &quot;the first line of defense against the Fae&quot; doesn't seem connected to the idea of &quot;giving them more range as characters&quot;.<br /> <br /> ... Wait...<br /> <br /> <br /> ... I'm feeling something of a mixed message here.<br /> </div> </div> </div>How exactly do those two things form a 'mixed message'?! 'Unique' means 'different from everybody else', it doesn't mean 'i only have this one thing' to-<br /> <br /> Ugh... Trying again...<br /> <br /> Okay, you know how Abyssals are described as servants of the Deathlords and champions of the dead, but they're not limited to JUST that role? It's like that. The Lunars had that in the 'shield wall against unreality' bits and I wish they'd done more of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:41:40-07:00","id":298123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298120#post298120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a fair bit of difference between 'Lunars are the only splat that has them as a primary threat woven into their history' (what i've been saying) and 'only Lunars ever fight them because otherwise Lunars suck' (what you seem to think I said) &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> How exactly do those two things form a 'mixed message'?! 'Unique' means 'different from everybody else', it doesn't mean 'i only have this one thing' to-<br /> <br /> Ugh... Trying again...<br /> <br /> Okay, you know how Abyssals are described as servants of the Deathlords and champions of the dead, but they're not limited to JUST that role? It's like that. The Lunars had that in the 'shield wall against unreality' bits and I wish they'd done more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bad example to pick for a metaphor, since the only options that Abyssals have is &quot;be servant of Deathlords or champion of death or stop being an Abyssal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:44:22-07:00","id":298125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298123#post298123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a bad example to pick for a metaphor, since the only options that Abyssals have is &quot;be servant of Deathlords or champion of death or stop being an Abyssal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the only one I've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:37:33-07:00","id":298173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298120#post298120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars had that in the 'shield wall against unreality' bits and I wish they'd done more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that &quot;shield wall against unreality&quot;, that is to say patrolling every border of <i>all of Creation</i>, is a hilariously impractical function even if you had all 300-ish guys working on it. And not in the &quot;well you just have to get good&quot; way either, the way where every Lunar spending all of their time on this one thing would still not be able to do it. Sidereals have a similarly impractical job, of course, but a major tenet of the Sidereal play experience is that they <i>aren't</i> getting everything done that they need to. And that's while being the single most unified and organized group among all Exalts. Lunars have the Silver Pact, but the Silver Pact itself is dubious as a &quot;racial identity&quot; in the first place, much less as something that can coordinate all of the Lunars with the efficiency that the Sidereals have.<br /> <br /> In order to give Lunars something that is actually theirs, I think you need to radically redefine at least part of the cosmology. The original setting has them as such an afterthought that trying to say &quot;well, they do this&quot; is trying to cram a square peg into a round hole. And apparently their shapeshifting doesn't cover that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:53:34-07:00","id":298186,"title":"","content":"I think it will help to let go of the idea that they (and the Solars and Dragon Blooded) have a kind of cosmically necessary function in the manner that Sidereals do, rather than a set of qualities that lead them to do things in distinct ways.<br /> <br /> Like the idea of what they do being &quot;basically anything, just in a manner you might expect from a shapeshifting monster hero&quot;. You have Solar pirates and Lunar pirates, and while the former act by being all exemplary at ship piloting and crew management and swinging between ships and generally swashbuckling, the latter do it by slipping off of the side of their schooners and torpedoing around beneath enemy ships, tearing out their keels, knocking holes in the hull and leaping over like Free Willy taking several sailors over the other side with them (things they may or may not do in an animal form).<br /> <br /> I think more milage might come out of that then trying to rope off &quot;special ops&quot; as some particular place for them.<br /> <br /> Likewise with the idea that one intrinsically needs Lunars in order to inject chaos into the world or keep Solars spontaneous or anything similar to that... that all still feels like stuff that Sidereals would be responsible for, even if there were occasions in which they'd look on Lunars as particularly useful ways of achieving that.<br /> <br /> I don't view the problem with &quot;the setting had no place for them&quot; in terms of whether there's some essential ontological niche they fill so much as the setting not acting as though there were four hundred terrifying, powerful, hunted beast saints from the previous age of the world running around, at least with any more consequence than &quot;occasionally Terrestrials on Wyld Hunts will fight them&quot;. Lunars don't need to have something they can do that other Exalts can't (in terms of achievements in the setting rather than expressions of their power), they just need something to give credibility to the idea that whatever others can do that fulfils the same function is irrelevant because it's not as if they're going anywhere.<br /> <br /> Which actually feels like an apt way to sum up the whole problem the Sidereals had with them in the Usurpation; they had a Prophecy concerning the Solars and Dragon Blooded and reordering the society of the world, and turned to the Lunars with a &quot;yeah, our vision for the future doesn't really have any place for you in it, so could you make things convenient and just go away forever please&quot;, and Lunars responding to that with scorn and laughter and flashing teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:54:48-07:00","id":298187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298120#post298120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Lunars are the only splat that has them as a primary threat woven into their history'</div> </div> </div> </div>Did people forget about the Balorian Crusade?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T09:02:34-07:00","id":298210,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hope that the origin of their Exaltation (Luna) plays a greater role in defining them as a group. After all, each Lunar meets him/her upon Exalting and Luna is a different sort of entity altogether from UCS and the Maidens. It would be interesting to see how Luna's other-worldliness and active interest in Creation would translate to his/her Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T11:58:10-07:00","id":298345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298210#post298210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely hope that the origin of their Exaltation (Luna) plays a greater role in defining them as a group. After all, each Lunar meets him/her upon Exalting and Luna is a different sort of entity altogether from UCS and the Maidens. It would be interesting to see how Luna's other-worldliness and active interest in Creation would translate to his/her Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always done it that Luna more than likely appears to the Lunar in the shape of their spirit animal, but in the purest of white and silver. She is of many shapes, and many minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T22:35:36-07:00","id":299723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=298187#post298187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did people forget about the Balorian Crusade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who?<br /> <br /> ( but more seriously, I only found any 2e books when i got bored waiting for 3e to roll around. That one is not one of them, sadly. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T08:49:16-08:00","id":301153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=299723#post299723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who?<br /> <br /> ( but more seriously, I only found any 2e books when i got bored waiting for 3e to roll around. That one is not one of them, sadly. )</div> </div> </div> </div>... that thing the raksha did after the Great Contagion. Led by some guy called Balor, apparently.<br /> It was one of those rare times when Sidereals, Lunars, and Dragonbloods agreed on killing something together (or at the very least, saving each other for last).<br /> And then after it was done, the usual oral histories and official testimonies were changed to make it seem like the Scarlet Empress did everything.<br /> <br /> You'd think they'd take this time to bond over their saving-the-world-without-Solars-thing, but no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:16:44-08:00","id":301185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=299723#post299723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who?<br /> <br /> ( but more seriously, I only found any 2e books when i got bored waiting for 3e to roll around. That one is not one of them, sadly. )</div> </div> </div> </div>....<br /> <br /> The Balorian Crusade is what happened when all of the Fair Folk got together and very nearly destroyed the world.<br /> <br /> As in &quot;an enormous portion of the world stopped existing after they were through with it&quot;, as well as how they came a hair's bredth away from polishing off the rest.<br /> <br /> This unhappy event formed the circumstances of the rise to power of the Scarlet Empress, and a fair amount of the rhetoric behind supporting her rule.<br /> <br /> The raksha are enemies to absolutely everybody. Even the Guild is more wary of them after that incident in the Scavenger Lands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:29:11-08:00","id":301269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=301185#post301185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The raksha are enemies to absolutely everybody. </div> </div> </div> </div>Most especially to the raksha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:17:38-08:00","id":305085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=301185#post301185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....<br /> <br /> The Balorian Crusade is what happened when all of the Fair Folk got together and very nearly destroyed the world.<br /> <br /> As in &quot;an enormous portion of the world stopped existing after they were through with it&quot;, as well as how they came a hair's bredth away from polishing off the rest.<br /> <br /> This unhappy event formed the circumstances of the rise to power of the Scarlet Empress, and a fair amount of the rhetoric behind supporting her rule.<br /> <br /> The raksha are enemies to absolutely everybody. Even the Guild is more wary of them after that incident in the Scavenger Lands.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... oh, THAT'S what that's called &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's SUPPOSED to be a huge event in the world's history but if we're honest, what did it really change? This might be because I've only gotten my hands on the Solar and Lunar splats, but it seems like the Balorian crusade is just a really big footnote as far as the setting's behavior today goes. Yeah, it brought the Scarlet Empress to power, but this era largely ignores the crusade. In the Solar splat it gets shoved to the side in favor of the Wyld hunt and other solars. I know the Fae are the enemy of everyone, I still like the idea that the Lunars see them as their primary foe. The two are not mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":879,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","user":"HalfTangible","date":". 11-06-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:25:20-08:00","id":305092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305085#post305085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... oh, THAT'S what that's called &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's SUPPOSED to be a huge event in the world's history but if we're honest, what did it really change? This might be because I've only gotten my hands on the Solar and Lunar splats, but it seems like the Balorian crusade is just a really big footnote as far as the setting's behavior today goes. Yeah, it brought the Scarlet Empress to power, but this era largely ignores the crusade. In the Solar splat it gets shoved to the side in favor of the Wyld hunt and other solars. I know the Fae are the enemy of everyone, I still like the idea that the Lunars see them as their primary foe. The two are not mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Contagion - a dual event which is made up of both the actual disease known as 'Great Contagion' on one hand, and the Fair Folk invasion led by Balor on the other - killed 90% of everything and destroyed vast swaths of the world. Entire nations were obliterated. The world was about to end. All who live today do so in its shadow. It cements the Fair Folk as the single most existential threat facing Creation today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:25:47-08:00","id":305093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305085#post305085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... oh, THAT'S what that's called &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's SUPPOSED to be a huge event in the world's history but if we're honest, what did it really change? This might be because I've only gotten my hands on the Solar and Lunar splats, but it seems like the Balorian crusade is just a really big footnote as far as the setting's behavior today goes. Yeah, it brought the Scarlet Empress to power, but this era largely ignores the crusade. In the Solar splat it gets shoved to the side in favor of the Wyld hunt and other solars. I know the Fae are the enemy of everyone, I still like the idea that the Lunars see them as their primary foe. The two are not mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inclination to see fae as the biggest problem probably ended when the chaos host's most powerful nobles ended up getting iron to the face courtesy of the Sword of Creation. In their state of disarray, they aren't doing anything cosmic or existential, and they aren't going anywhere except to the Guild to basically binge drink themselves into a stupor. Any threats which the fae pose are highly individual, like the one noble who imitates Lunar hunting practices and goes out of her way to try and seek out and provoke Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:29:48-08:00","id":305095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305085#post305085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... oh, THAT'S what that's called &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's SUPPOSED to be a huge event in the world's history but if we're honest, what did it really change? This might be because I've only gotten my hands on the Solar and Lunar splats, but it seems like the Balorian crusade is just a really big footnote as far as the setting's behavior today goes. Yeah, it brought the Scarlet Empress to power, but this era largely ignores the crusade. In the Solar splat it gets shoved to the side in favor of the Wyld hunt and other solars. I know the Fae are the enemy of everyone, I still like the idea that the Lunars see them as their primary foe. The two are not mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it caused widespread horrible Wyld mutations, caused the Fair Folk to be an even more constant threat, and caused pockets of isolated Wyld in Creation, destabilizing it. The Fae aren't always the enemy of everyone, but they occupy that space easily. Many have &quot;gone native&quot; and feed off of Creation and mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:11:01-08:00","id":305332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305092#post305092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Contagion - a dual event which is made up of both the actual disease known as 'Great Contagion' on one hand, and the Fair Folk invasion led by Balor on the other - killed 90% of everything and destroyed vast swaths of the world. Entire nations were obliterated. The world was about to end. All who live today do so in its shadow. It cements the Fair Folk as the single most existential threat facing Creation today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are they always in the background?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:44:42-08:00","id":305411,"title":"","content":"Who told that they are always in the background? They are a constant threat and main antogonist in many campains. But since creation has so many enemies, neverborn, yozi , fae and good old internal strugle &amp; civil war its hard to pick only one and go...from my point of few Fae when used in this fashion are the most bland of foes, hence you dont see them taking the stage all that often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T02:26:51-08:00","id":305461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305085#post305085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's SUPPOSED to be a huge event in the world's history but if we're honest, what did it really change?</div> </div> </div> </div>It changed all of Creation from a tumultuous oligarchy of several hundred thousand Dragon Blooded fighting over large, but dwindling, caches of the legacy of the First Age, into the huge mess of competing states and fringe barbarians and terrible wilderness with an autocracy consisting of a few thousand Dragon Blooded lying in the centre trying to keep the whole thing from falling apart completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> this era largely ignores the crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The popular image of the Fair Folk throughout all of Creation is of an endless teeming mass of howling terrors waiting to destroy all of the world. It's an image that haunts all of those who live under the threat of the raksha. It is, in fact, a significant basis of the propaganda of the Realm; the claim that, should the power of the Empress fall, they'll come back to finish the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280860-why-do-you-like-lunars?p=305332#post305332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why are they always in the background?</div> </div> </div> </div>Always? Do you mean always in the two books you apparently have?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:46:42-08:00","id":305628,"title":"","content":"OH FORGET IT!!! Fine, Lunars suck and there's nothing at all I like about them since apparently it's invalid to like the only thing in their book that didn't completely suck.<br /> <br /> Happy now? Sure hope so. Goodbye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>D